# The rank-two local application of A.3.18

For the literal H = KLᵥ and C = K.subgroupOf H, the source setup yields
SQTK, C-component placement, three-rank two, and quasisimplicity of C/O₂(C)
with center of three-rank at most one. The same intrinsic statements are
exported for K, as required by the enclosing residual-case proof.

The actual image R in H/O₃′(H) is quasisimple. Its central quotient is
compared with that of the literal plus image K+, compatibly with both
quotient maps on elements of K. All these conclusions are constructed.
The universal A.3.6 and A.3.12 clauses and genuine earlier source data
remain explicit; the enclosing owner retains their discharge and the
A.3.18 case analysis leading to theta and containment.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript, 13.6.20, p.931,
and A.3.18, pp.51–53.
